## Why hold telemetry, not an initial report run lock

scoped_reports230/398–399 drops the initial PathTx on output refusal, then
scoped_output_refusal32 reacquires a full RunTx. Queueing a drain behind the
initial path report does not force report commit first. Instead block the actual
refusal's root telemetry upsert while it ALREADY owns the run: refusal86–101 /
PGexecution4230–4249. No telemetry row is inserted/updated by fixture SQL.

Before concurrency, existing migration/source/authority checks, normal Keeper
renewal, original live uncancelled c10[0]/reserve, scopeOPEN/no stop/failure/Return/
free slot and E4200020. Require zero selected-run chain membership. Capture v0,
complete existing execution footprint and telemetry row head=v0.
Create separate role-correct max1 PgRunStore scheduler pool, fresh cache and same
real Keeper placement; capture its backendPID S/database/current_user. Keep its
pool alive and its backend identified. All participants use actual owner or
sagat_app URLs derived from the exact owned fixture. No permissions are widened.
Initialize Metrics::global before race; capture relevant existing counters.

## Two observed blocking edges and actual typed CAS

Owner administrative holder tx locks selected tenant/run telemetry_pending row
FOR UPDATE; capturePID H. Send unchanged retained original complete_step via a
cloned current authenticated client, retaining its JoinHandle. No new worker,
registration, poll, key, renewal, rebuilt report or capability edit.
Observe exactly one actual API-role report backend R active/Lock at native
telemetry upsert and blocked byH. Use fresh autocommit observer queries through
API-role pool (same role sessions visible); match db/user/queryshape/PID/edges,
not generic lock counts or whole session dumps. Report actor remains held there.
Committed full footprint must still equal prestate; uncommitted stop is invisible.

Launch actual public scheduler.advance_collection using dedicated actorS. Its
read-only repeatable-read frontier sees old v0/no stop/E; native start-drain then
blocks on run owned byR. Require S active/Lock at EXACT native drain SQL selecting
namespace_id,workflow_version_id,run_version,status,stop_reason,stop_code,paused
FROM runs ... FOR UPDATE (primitives648–684). A full-run fallback waits at a
different query and is a failure. Recheck both H→R and R→S blocking edges together,
known actors/databases/roles/queryshapes and unchanged committed footprint.

Only after both edges, ROLLBACK holder. Join actual report and scheduler under
bounded deadlines. Report must deliver accepted original SUCCEEDED/CANCELLING ACK.
Scheduler MUST return CollectionAdvanceError::Primitive(PrimitiveStoreError::
RevisionConflict{current:v1}); no retry/fallback, Waiting/Skipped/arbitrary error.
v1>v0 and v1 equals independently persisted head, receipt revision and ACK revision.
Native drain checks revision before evidence/mutation (primitives2494/687–696);
public advance propagates it (passes1830–1837), while tick would hide it asSkipped.

## Exact post-report and fresh decision

Before ANY fresh scheduling, existing actual refusal/receipt/footprint helpers
prove one FAILED/RDL stop before one original genuine completed success/nooutput,
original attempt/generation/worker actor/reported hash, original uncancelled lease
settledSUCCEEDED, scopeOPEN/memberADMITTED/heldslot, original source/authority/
reservations/retained outputs. One exact report receipt/refusal audit/originaltrace;
no candidate payload/blob/charge/forward release/Return/drain/compensation, no
outbox delta. Run/journal/telemetry head=v1. No effect belongs to rejected CAS.
Existing helper names may be narrowly generalized; preserve prior assertions.

Fresh store/cache public advance MUST DrainStarted. It selects
stopped_for_run_data_limit before E, preserving original stop/seq. Exactly one
new drain event/hint and stopped-for-limit audit; zero existing_outputs/aggregate
audit from the stale command. Exact order stop→completion→drain and original
trace/identity/source. Metric refusal+1 on report, primitiveRDL+0 for stale CAS,
then+1 for fresh drain; no invented CAS metric.

Rejoin accepted report-first body: original canonical replay; one actual
line.release targeting original instance/key; held compensation cannot finalize;
real completion, COMPENSATED/FAILED-RDL/DONE-COMPENSATED, terminal original ACK
replay and fresh_verify. Apply existing stronger pending and terminal replay
oracles currently under-limit-only to CAS too; no weakening original presets.
E4200020, original source/payload/authority witnesses stay exact throughout.

## Bounded error cleanup is part of proof

Choose explicit small finite observation/query/join budgets inside existing300s
phase bound; actor statement timeout must exceed combined observation budget.
Reuse timeout+yield_now barrier pattern (durable-execution/concurrency234–256),
never sleeps. Fresh autocommit stats observations avoid transaction snapshots.
Never assert/panic while holder is retained: collect proof Result, rollback holder
on every path, then surface errors only AFTER actor cleanup. Existing witness
helpers that panic must run in an owned joined task or equivalent capture so an
unexpected read failure still releases holder. Keep all actor handles; aborting
a client alone does not prove the server stopped. After rollback, bounded-join
both actors, verify their server transactions are closed, then close dedicated
pool. If cleanup requires cancelling a known actor backend, use only identified
owned PID after barrier release, record failure, and never count it as CAS success.
On failure before reportPID identification, release holder first and ensure
bounded API/server shutdown/pool closure; retain safe evidence, no loose actors.
No sql state/status/lease/receipt/output edits, sleeps, alternate success or retry
on mutated handoff. Real timeout/query/error/cleanup failure stops acceptance.

## Sources and root gates

PG16 READ COMMITTED may lock the row version committed by a concurrent updater;
separate read-only frontier retains its own earlier snapshot. Root verified
[isolation](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/transaction-iso.html).
Use fresh stats reads, observing only sessions of the participant role; root
verified [visibility/snapshots](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/monitoring-stats.html).
Blocking PIDs can include earlier incompatible waiters, so query and both edges
are required; root verified [blocking semantics](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/functions-info.html).

